**Job description and purpose:**

The Aristotle Foundation for Public Policy is an educational and public policy think tank in Canada that began public operations in 2023\. We champion reason, democracy, and civilization. We seek to anchor Canadian ideas and public life in facts and informed history. We like to make people think.

We are hiring a Vice President of Operations to help us renew Canada. The details and duties are below.

**About the Aristotle Foundation and why we matter**

The civilization we now possess grew from debates about the “good life” and the stirrings of democracy in ancient Greece, Jewish monotheism, and the influence of “Rome.” It was nourished by the Middle Ages, Magna Carta, the Reformation, the Glorious Revolution, the Renaissance, and the Enlightenment. Our world also came about because of 18th\- and 19th\-century thinkers including Adam Smith, Edmund Burke, John Stuart Mill, and Mary Wollstonecraft among others.

We are all fortunate that brave men and women in past centuries initiated popular movements for reform—abolitionists, suffragettes, and those who battled for civil rights for all.

All that and more resulted in a civilization worth cherishing and renewing.

That’s why our vision for Canada is one where the sacrifices and successes of past generations are cherished and built upon; where citizens value each other for their character and merit; and where open inquiry and free expression are prized as the best path to a flourishing future for all.

Since our public launch in 2023, the Aristotle Foundation for Public Policy has improved Canada’s idea debates. We have done so by publishing high\-quality research and by relentlessly marketing our work to the public. We have published best\-selling books, dozens of studies and videos, hundreds of columns and over 1,000 infographics. Our work has appeared in the pages of the National Post, the Toronto Star, the Globe and Mail, and other new and traditional media across Canada. Our fresh take means our work often goes viral on social media.

A registered charity, we are donor\-funded and neither seek nor would accept government funding, so that we retain our independence. We are based in Calgary, with staff and scholars across Canada.

We have grown quickly in impact, output, staff, scholars, followers, and financial support. And we have only just started.

**About the Role: Help Us Make Canada Civilized, Sane, and Prosperous**

Here is the leader we want to hire: a complement to the president, and vice versa. You will be the ultimate integrator. You value bringing visionary ideas to fruition and impact. You are passionate about working in a think tank that aims to double its budget, staff, scholars, and output—but more important than any of that, to expand its David\-like impact exponentially in a world of Goliaths. Together with the President, you will enable the organization to hit new heights through exponential growth by ensuring efficient internal operations.

Specifically, you possess these qualities and skills:

* passionate about managing people to bring out the best in them;
* an intuitive and practical grasp of people—their character, challenges, frustrations, and hopes and dreams;
* a conceptual thinker;
* eager to run day\-to\-day operations;
* steady, and able to integrate the major functions of the organization harmoniously;
* able to create organizational lucidity so the right hand knows what the left hand is doing;
* the voice of reason;
* able to implement a plan practically, bring it to fruition, and achieve goals;
* focused, detail\-oriented, and excellent at developing and nourishing talent;
* personally accountable, adept at self\-management, and decisive;
* a catalyst for team cohesion; a strong leader and manager; and an effective conflict manager;
* resilient, adaptable, forward\-thinking, persuasive, a problem solver, continuous learner, and able to understand and evaluate others.

Specifically, here’s what you like to provide and can achieve:

* clarity;
* communication;
* resolution;
* focus;
* accountability;
* team unity;
* follow\-through and well\-managed projects;
* an end to obstacles and barriers;
* prioritization and execution;
* steadiness, cadence, and consistency;
* day\-to\-day tasks that run smoothly;
* execution of the strategic plan;
* the glue that holds everything and everyone together, including harmonious integration of the leadership team;
* harnessing visionary ideas and ensuring everything and everyone is pointed in the same direction;
* being the tiebreaker that keeps things moving.

If you are successful, this will free the president to focus on three priorities: strategy; meeting with supporters; and public\-facing work.

The VP of Operations will own the operational backbone of the organization—ensuring all departments run smoothly and work together so our small team can scale efficiently while remaining lean and focused on impact.

This role requires close, day\-to\-day partnership with the President. The President maintains high standards and is highly particular about quality, process, and alignment with the Foundation’s mission. The VP of Operations is expected to provide responsiveness, and proactive support so the President’s priorities are executed effectively.

This role can potentially be remote at first, but eventually the vice president will need to be in Calgary. It will also require travel.

**Key Responsibilities**

* Oversee internal day\-to\-day operations, systems, and processes supporting the Aristotle Foundation’s team.
* Ensure Research, Marketing, and Philanthropy departments are running as they should and meeting expectations and targets.
* Support donor relations and development operations, including CRM management and reporting.
* Manage finance, budgeting, charity compliance (CRA), contracts, and basic HR/people operations for a small team.
